From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 23:42:42 -0500
Subject: fix: little windows, the rest

A little window closed by hand now goes on the list Shift-Cmd-T reads and
comes back little. A popup was never recorded, so the keys brought back
whatever had been closed before it. A rule whose Space is gone no longer holds
a link back from a little window; it routes nothing (routing D14).

In a window with tabs and no Spaces, Option-Cmd-Left and Right and Cmd-D did
nothing, because Spaces took those keys from Chromium. They step through the
tabs and make a bookmark there, as Chromium's did.
On the Mac the Spaces menu's pin row, which carries Cmd-D, stays enabled
there as the command is; it was enabled only with Spaces, so the key found
it disabled and did nothing.

Why: the rest of S-157 (little E13, shortcuts Z24, PLAN.md CMD-18).

Removable when: little windows or private windows stop being separate kinds of
window.
